// THE STREET — the fiction layer.
// Three rules from the narrative design are enforced here instead of remembered:
//   1. No line is ever spoken by the game. Every one has a neighbour's name in front of
//      it — a narrator saying sharing is good is a sermon, a person complaining is not.
//   2. Somebody permanently disagrees. That is RUI, and he is why the sincere lines are
//      allowed to be sincere.
//   3. NO AUTHORED STRING CONTAINS A DIGIT. That keeps invented text from ever being
//      mistaken for the sourced REAL DATA banner, and test/smoke.js asserts it. The
//      numbers in the epilogue are interpolated from the run at render time; none of
//      them is written down in this section.
// It is 2026 and this is a street, not a court: mutirão, a shared pot, a painted wall.
// ============================================================


