// the middle of the picture is. It used to be near-white — L 214 sick, 231 healed, C* under
// 9 — which meant the ridge, the town and the far treeline all arrived somewhere paler than
// the sky in front of them and with the colour bleached out of them. The board does neither:
// its far end of the street measures [132,115,87], L 117 at C* 21, and the haze band over
// its rooftops is L 144 at C* 16. So: a hazy warm green when healed, a bleached warm ochre
// when sick, both a value BELOW the top of the sky and both carrying real chroma. Still
// light relative to the near plane — that is the value architecture — just not white.
// ...and it is the SCENARIO'S, for the same reason the sky ramp below is: what the distance
// dissolves into is the bottom of that place's sky seen through that place's air. A street
// dissolves into hazy warm green; a coast dissolves into salt light off water.
