// ---------- THE TWO AUTHORED PALETTES ----------
// Every colour in the world used to be a `lerpC(sickPair, healedPair, h)` written at the
// point of use — about forty of them, scattered. Each pair was authored at its two ENDS and
// nobody ever authored the middle, so an intermediate world was forty unrelated straight
// lines through RGB space arriving wherever they arrived. And a straight RGB line between a
// bleached ochre and a saturated green passes through grey: that is literally where the mud
// came from.
//
// Two named palettes now, one sick and one healed, resolved once per health step. The
// interpolation is not a straight line — it is split into the two channels the direction
// actually cares about:
//   · VALUE moves linearly, because the parallax planes are separated by value and that
//     separation has to hold at every t, not just at the ends;
//   · CHROMA is carried on the HEALED hue the whole way and only its amount ramps, so a
//     half-healed world is a faded photograph of the healed one — never a third colour that
//     nobody drew. That is "the arc runs on saturation" made literal.
// Aerial perspective is folded in here too (each entry carries its own distance), so a
// drawing call is one string lookup instead of a mix plus a haze plus a format.
