// hero croma 73 -> 149 of 485 at MANHÃ, dE 29 -> 40, luma 35 -> 49. The framing is worth
// keeping and the bill is not, and the two come apart, because what rivals him is not the
// tree's MASS — a flat mass scores near zero, which is the whole reason the framing measure
// had to be rewritten in wave 11 — it is the tree's SATURATION standing against open sky.
// So the mass stays to the pixel and the colour steps back one plane: this crown is the one
// green in the picture with nothing but sky behind it, which is exactly the thing aerial
// perspective acts on. Same five colours, same construction, one desaturation, done once at
// load and in BASE colours so `wc` still applies the hour exactly once.
// A MIX TOWARD BRILHO WAS THE FIRST CUT AND THE PRINT REFUSED IT. It measured well — at 0.42
// his croma went 149 -> 100 — but it works by LIGHTENING, so the crown came out paler than
// the ridges behind it, and a near tree paler than the far hill inverts the depth of the
