// ---------- DECORAÇÕES ----------
// The board devotes a whole strip to them, and it is the strip that decides whether a street
// reads as somewhere people live or as a backdrop with a character standing in front of it:
// benches, a street lamp, potted plants, a washing line strung with clothes, planters,
// chairs. All of them wood, terracotta and FOLHAS — nothing new enters the palette. They are
// placed the way the board composes them, which is dense but never a uniform row: each one
// sits at its own offset inside the segment, and no segment gets more than one.
// Every colour here goes through the hour, on the same 24 steps the hero and the neighbours
// use. It is not decoration on the decoration: the first night screenshot had a bench glowing
// warm brown out of a dark street, because a hard-coded hex does not know what time it is.
// Only what is actually a light source — the lamp's glass and its spill — is left alone.
