// ---------- the wand, and the light it channels ----------
// He carries no blade. The magic here is folk magic — tending and mending, the same hand
// that plants a sprout — so its colours are the world's own: amber at the core, going out
// through warm gold into the green of new growth. Never cold, never arcane-purple.
