// but not the same dose the world takes, because two things have to survive it:
//   · HE HAS TO STAY READABLE AT PHONE SIZE. The world's dimming (`escala`, 0.44 at NOITE)
//     would sink a 22 px character into the ground plane. His is FLOORED — a third of the
//     way back to full — and the hour's tint reaches him at 80% strength, so night moves
//     him a long way in hue and only a little in value. He goes cool and quiet; he never
//     goes to a silhouette.
//   · THE CETRO STAYS THE BRIGHTEST THING IN A DARK FRAME. Its wood takes an even gentler
//     dose (floored more than half way, tint at 45%), and the lit hub, the crystal and
//     everything `luz()` draws are not touched by the hour at all. So as the street goes
